$save — export the last bundle item to a named file

SUMMARY
  Copies the last link from the array that matches the destination file
  extension into op/saved/<filename> and appends that path to files[].

SYNTAX
  $save('output.mp4')
  $save(path='result.png')

INPUT
  Uses the last element of the array implied by the output extension:
    .mp4 → videos[]
    .png, .jpg, .jpeg → images[]
    .mp3 → sounds[]
    .txt → texts[]
    other → files[]

OUTPUT
  files[] — link to the saved copy under op/saved/

BEHAVIOR
  If the source array is empty, writes a small placeholder text file instead.
  Other input arrays are passed through unchanged.

EXAMPLE
  @gen_clip: (@images, @track) -> $image_clip -> $save('output.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
